{"id": "3ba2bdbe-3872-4c5c-864c-c7b5065254e6", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T03:27:09.469802", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "1e1dbe4b-5e3e-4f3b-affa-e8a152855b4d", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-f5f37027-c2c6-4084-8c30-ab4e75caf130", "tool_call": {"id": "call-f5f37027-c2c6-4084-8c30-ab4e75caf130", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Propose experimental design (plan stage)\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"## What I found in /workspace (as-is)\\n\\nThe workspace is effectively empty of source materials. `inspect_repository` and three recursive finds (`-iname '*infllm*'`, `'*README*'`, `'*paper*'`, `'track.md'`) returned:\\n\\n- `/workspace/task.json` (433 bytes) — the only project file. It restates the public question, names a `documents.track.md` whose value is the placeholder string *\\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"*, and sets environment/runtime flags (`bubblewrap`, `network: disabled`, no GPU, 24 CPUs, no preinstalled deps, no datasets).\\n- Empty `/workspace/`: no README, no notes, no InfLLM paper, no code excerpts, no config files, no scripts, no datasets.\\n- The only false-positive `README` / `paper` matches are OS files (`/lib/ispell/README.select-ispell`, `/lib/locale/LC_PAPER`, ubuntu-wallpapers docs, `/usr/local/cuda-13.1/README`) — none are project content.\\n- Runtime: Python 3.12.3 present; the task system itself explicitly states compute is not required and the deliverable is design-only.\\n\\n**Implication for fidelity:** I have no in-repo reference implementation of InfLLM. The design below is constructed from public-description knowledge of InfLLM as a training-free KV-cache memory architecture (cached \\\"memory\\\" units of past context + dynamic top-k retrieval into the live attention window). I am flagging this as Assumption A1 / Uncertainty U1 below.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Proposed approach\\n\\n**Research question recap.** How much of InfLLM's long-context performance comes from (a) the *dynamic memory-lookup mechanism itself* (vs. fixed/sliding-window baselines) and (b) the *granularity/unit representation* of what is stored and retrieved?\\n\\n**Core design.** A controlled, factorial ablation on a **single frozen base long-context LM**, varying two axes orthogonally and adding targeted extension cells:\\n\\n**Axis 1 — Lookup mechanism `L` (memory access policy)**\\n| Cell | Description | Purpose |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| L0 | **No-retrieval baseline** — full-context attention (truncated to budget) or positional-interpolation only | Lower-bound performance |\\n| L1 | **Fixed/recurrent cache** — keep first-N tokens always in memory, evict the rest | Fixed-memory ablation |\\n| L2 | **Sliding window** — keep last-W tokens in attention, recompute rest | Standard efficient-attention baseline |\\n| L3 | **InfLLM-style dynamic lookup** (reference) — cached memory units + per-step top-k retrieval into live window | Reference behavior |\\n| L4 | L3 with **retrieval-frequency sweep** — every 1 / 4 / 16 / 64 generated tokens | Isolates cost–quality curve |\\n| L5 | L3 with **retrieval disabled at depth ≥ D** (off in middle, on at extremes) | Diagnostic on where the dynamic component matters |\\n\\n**Axis 2 — Unit representation `U` (what is embedded/cached/retrieved)**\\n| Cell | Description | Pooling / similarity |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| U_T | **Token-level** — 1 token = 1 unit, KV cached per token | KV re-use; similarity = dot-product on hidden state |\\n| U_B | **Block-level** — contiguous blocks of 16 / 64 / 256 tokens (sweep as sub-axis) | Mean-pool hidden state for the *query* representation; cosine similarity; KV block re-used across retrieved block |\\n| U_S | **Sentence-level** — offline-segmented sentences | Mean-pool; cosine |\\n| U_G | **Block + learned/analytic cross-attention gate** — block embeddings feed a scalar gate computed at attention time | Adds a third hyperparameter (gate temperature) without retraining if analytic |\\n\\nThese two axes define the **primary 2×2 cores**: (L0×U_B), (L3×U_T), (L3×U_B), (L2×U_B). The remaining cells are extension ablations to explain *why* a core cell wins or loses.\\n\\n**Orthogonal micro-axis — similarity metric (cosine / dot-product / learned gate)** is folded into U_B for A4.3 (cross-attention gates) and reported as a sub-cell rather than a third full axis to keep the design within budget.\\n\\n### What is measured\\n\\n**Task battery (capabilities)**\\n1. **Passkey retrieval** — RULER-style single-fact hidden in noise. The most sensitive probe for memory lookup.\\n2. **Needle-in-a-Haystack (NIAH)** at multiple depths / distractors / multiple needles.\\n3. **Multi-hop QA** — long-context variants of HotpotQA and 2WikiMultihopQA; reasoning across separated facts.\\n4. **Long-context summarization** — GovReport / SQuALITY / a single long-document QA set the researcher prefers. ROUGE-L + LLM-judge faithfulness as secondary.\\n\\n**Per-step diagnostic metrics (this is where the question actually gets answered)**\\n- **Retrieval precision@K, recall@K** at each lookup step (only meaningful when L ∈ {L3, L4, L5} or U ∈ {U_B, U_S, U_G} defines retrievable units).\\n- **Hit rate at true passage** for passkey/NIAH, decomposed by depth bin (0–25%, 25–50%, 50–75%, 75–100% of context).\\n- **Open-book perplexity** on held-out long-context LM-evaluation corpora (PG-19, ArXiv-math, CodeParrot) with the memory budget fixed.\\n\\n**System metrics**\\n- End-to-end **latency** (ms/token, mean and P95).\\n- **KV-cache footprint (GB)** at each length.\\n- **Retrieval compute** (% of total step time, FLOP share).\\n\\n### Controls (fixed across all cells)\\n- **Same base model, frozen weights.** Suggested default: an open long-context LM with ≥128k native window (e.g., LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct, Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct-1M). Researcher to confirm.\\n- **Identical context length** within each length-sweep point (4k / 16k / 64k / 128k; the 128k point becomes analytically tractable / downsampled if compute is tight — see Feasibility).\\n- **Identical prompts, decoding settings, seeds** for any stochastic component (block sampling, gate noise).\\n- **Matched retrieval budget per cell.** All dynamic-lookup variants are given the same wall-clock retrieval budget per step (top-K with K chosen so that total retrieval FLOPs across cells differs by ≤10%). All non-dynamic baselines receive an \\\"equivalent budget\\\" by being allowed the same wall-clock step.\\n- **Matched training data.** For LLM cells the method is training-free. The only trainable component is a *cross-attention gate* (U_G); if included, it is trained on a fixed corpus slice with a fixed seed/epochs and held out of evaluation.\\n- **Identical KV representation.** No positional encoding tricks beyond what the base model already uses; RoPE scaling held constant.\\n\\n### Analysis plan\\n- **Primary contrast:** the **2×2 core factorial** (`lookup ∈ {off, dynamic}` × `unit ∈ {token, block}`) at each length, with the dynamic cell instantiated as L3 + U_B and block size = 16.\\n- **Extension contrasts:** length sweep × L cells × U cells, reported as a heatmap (accuracy on task × length × condition).\\n- **Length sweep:** 4k, 16k, 64k, 128k. Truncate 128k to 64k for any sub-task that does not support longer inputs (TBD by researcher).\\n- **Statistical reporting.** ≥3 seeds per cell on tasks with non-deterministic bookkeeping (none expected for inference, but addresses order effects in retrieval). **Paired bootstrap** of (variant − baseline) over tasks × contexts × seeds; **Bonferroni–Holm** correction across the metric set; report mean ± 95% CI and **Cohen's d** for each primary contrast; pre-register the primary contrast before opening data.\\n- **Ablation decomposition.** When U_B beats U_T, independently vary (i) chunk size and (ii) similarity metric to localize the gain. When L3 beats L2, run L4 / L5 to localize it to retrieval *coverage* vs *frequency*.\\n\\n### Feasibility (design-only, no execution claimed)\\n- **In scope for this deliverable.** Specification of cells, controls, metrics, statistical plan, risks. The track explicitly notes compute is not required and successful exploration is **not** proof of execution (per env note).\\n- **If executed at pilot scale.** One core 2×2 × 1 length × 2 tasks would be the minimum informative slice. Wall-clock estimate on a single A100/H100 for ~1B-token LM at 64k context, 3 seeds, 4 cells, 4 tasks: rough order 10s of GPU-hours (no parallelism is required, just a budget envelope). With retrieval-frequency × length, full sweep multiplies this by ~5–8×.\\n- **Offline / analytically tractable decomposition.** The U-axis (unit/pooling/similarity) and the L4 retrieval-frequency sweep are runnable on a *fixed short context* (4k–8k) using only retrieval-quality metrics (precision@K, recall@K) and passkey — no real long-context generation needed. This gives an early signal at near-zero cost.\\n- **Compute budget tiers.** Tier-1 (core 2×2, length = 16k, 4 tasks, 3 seeds) ≈ minimum confident answer. Tier-2 adds length sweep. Tier-3 adds L4, L5, U_G learned-gate training. Each tier inherits from the prior.\\n\\n### Consequential assumptions (separate from task requirements)\\n- **A1 — InfLLM mechanism.** I describe it as a training-free KV-cache architecture with cached memory units and dynamic top-k retrieval per attention step, with retention/eviction of distant tokens. *The exact published retention rule, eviction schedule, top-k schedule, and \\\"training-free\\\" claim should be reconfirmed against the paper before any claim of \\\"matches/fails-to-match InfLLM\\\" is made.*\\n- **A2 — Base model.** A frozen open long-context LM with ≥128k native window is selectable; the researcher may prefer a specific one (e.g., the one used in the InfLLM paper itself).\\n- **A3 — Training condition for the gate (U_G).** Designing U_G analytically (Section 3.4 cross-attention gate formula) is preferred; if learned, training corpus size / epochs are fixed across variants.\\n- **A4 — \\\"Memory\\\" definition.** Cached past K/V units indexed by hidden-state query; not parametric memory injection.\\n- **A5 — Evaluation harness.** Tasks listed are defaults and interchangeable; the researcher may pin specific ones.\\n\\n### Uncertainties to resolve before result stage\\n- **U1 — Reference fidelity.** Without the paper PDF / repo in the workspace, the *reference* cell (L3×U_B) is a reconstruction from public description. I can reduce this with one of: (i) researcher provides the paper text or URL excerpt, (ii) we label the reference cell explicitly as \\\"spec-faithful-pending-confirmation.\\\"\\n- **U2 — Base model choice.** Affects absolute numbers but not the comparative answer.\\n- **U3 — Length-sweep ceiling.** 128k feasibility depends on VRAM; I will mark it Tier-3 if asked.\\n- **U4 — Whether to include a learned gate (trains extra parameters).** Affects the \\\"matched training data\\\" control.\\n- **U5 — Statistical unit.** Whether the researcher prefers paired bootstrap across items vs across seeds (n differs by orders of magnitude).\\n- **U6 — Whether retrieval-frequency (L4) belongs in Tier-1 (core) or Tier-2 (extension).**\",\"evidence\":\"Repository inspection (inspect_repository on /workspace and three recursive finds for *infllm*, *README*, *paper*, *track.md*) returned a single project file, /workspace/task.json (433 bytes), whose own `documents.track.md` field is a placeholder stating compute is not required and the design is the deliverable. All README/paper hits were unrelated OS files (ispell, locale, cuda docs, ubuntu-wallpapers). Python 3.12.3 is present; the environment block in task.json declares bubblewrap, no GPU, 24 CPUs, disabled network, no preinstalled deps, no datasets. No InfLLM paper, code, configs, READMEs, notes, or scripts were found anywhere in the workspace, so the design is constructed from public-description knowledge of InfLLM (training-free KV-cache memory architecture with dynamic top-k retrieval) with that gap flagged as Assumption A1 / Uncertainty U1.\",\"assumptions\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"A5 Default task battery (passkey / NIAH / multi-hop QA / long summarization) is interchangeable if researcher prefers alternatives.</item>\\n\",\"$text\":\"A4 \\\"Memory\\\" = cached past K/V units indexed by hidden-state query; not parametric memory injection.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"A3 Training-free policy holds for L0–L3; U_G gate is preferred analytic; if it is learned it uses a fixed corpus slice with fixed seed/epochs.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"A2 A single frozen open long-context LM (≥128k native window) is used as the base for all cells.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"A1 InfLLM described as training-free KV-cache architecture with cached memory units + per-step dynamic top-k retrieval. (Pending reconfirmation against paper.)</item>\\n\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"U6 Whether retrieval-frequency sweep (L4) is core (Tier-1) or extension (Tier-2).</item>\\n\",\"$text\":\"U5 Preferred statistical unit (items vs seeds) for paired bootstrap.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U4 Whether to include a learned cross-attention gate (U_G) which would require controlled training.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U3 Length-sweep ceiling at 128k tokens depends on VRAM; may be moved to Tier-3.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U2 Base model identity — affects absolute performance but not the comparative interpretation.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U1 Reference fidelity of the L3×U_B cell to the published InfLLM specification, since no paper or code is in the workspace.</item>\\n\"}]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-ea5b1b8f-ae54-4613-9aa7-d0aaedca0356", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 12}
