truct-1M). Researcher to confirm.\\n- Identical context length within each length-sweep point (4k / 16k / 64k / 128k; 128k may be downscoped \\u2014 see Feasibility).\\n- Identical prompts, decoding settings, seeds for any stochastic component (block sampling, gate noise).\\n- Matched retrieval budget per cell. All dynamic-lookup variants given the same wall-clock retrieval budget per step (top-K tuned so total retrieval FLOPs across cells differs by \\u226410%). Non-dynamic baselines receive an equivalent wall-clock step.\\n- Matched training data. Inference-time methods need no training; the only trainable component is the U_G cross-attention gate \\u2014 if included, it is trained on a fixed corpus slice with fixed seed/epochs and held-out of evaluation.\\n- Identical KV representation. No positional-encoding tricks beyond the base model; RoPE scaling held constant.\\n\\n### Analysis plan\\n- Primary contrast: the 2\\u00d72 core factorial (`lookup \\u2208 {off, dynamic}` \\u00d7 `unit \\u2208 {token, block}`) at each length; the dynamic cell instantiated as L3 + U_B with block size = 16.\\n- Extension contrasts: length sweep \\u00d7 L cells \\u00d7 U cells, reported as a heatmap (accuracy \\u00d7 task \\u00d7 length \\u00d7 condition).\\n- Length sweep: 4k, 16k, 64k, 128k. Truncate 128k to 64k for sub-tasks that do not support longer inputs.\\n- Statistical reporting. \\u22653 seeds per cell on tasks with non-deterministic bookkeeping (none expected for inference but covers any order-effect in retrieval). Paired bootstrap of (variant \\u2212 baseline) over tasks \\u00d7 contexts \\u00d7 seeds; Bonferroni\\u2013Holm correction across the metric set; report mean \\u00b1 95% CI and Cohen's d for each primary contrast; pre-register primary contrast before opening data.\\n- Ablation decomposition. When U_B beats U_T, independently vary (i) chunk size and (ii) similarity metric to localize the gain. When L3 beats L2, run L4/L5 to localize the win to retrieval coverage vs retrieval frequency.\\n\\n### Feasibility (design-only, no execution claimed)\\n- In scope for this deliverable. Specification of cells, controls, metrics, statistical plan, risks. The track itself notes compute is not required and successful exploration is not proof of execution (per env note).\\n- If executed at pilot scale. One core 2\\u00d72 \\u00d7 1 length \\u00d7 2 tasks is the minimum informative slice. Wall-clock estimate on a single A100/H100 for ~1B-token LM at 64k context, 3 seeds, 4 cells, 4 tasks: rough order 10s of GPU-hours (no parallelism required). The full sweep (L4, length sweep) multiplies by ~5\\u20138\\u00d7.\\n- Offline / analytic tractable decomposition. The U-axis (unit/pooling/similarity) and the L4 retrieval-frequency sweep are runnable on a *fixed short context* (4k\\u20138k) using only retrieval-quality metrics (precision@K, recall@K) and passkey \\u2014 no real long-context generation. Early signal at near-zero cost.\\n- Compute tiers. Tier-1 = core 2\\u00d72 \\u00d7 length = 16k \\u00d7 4 tasks \\u00d7 3 seeds (minimum confident answer). Tier-2 adds the length sweep. Tier-3 adds L4, L5, and U_G learned-gate training. Each tier inherits from the prior.\", \"evidence\": \"Repository inspection (inspect_repository on /workspace plus three recursive finds for *infllm*, *README*, *paper*, *track.md`) returned one project file: /workspace/task.json (433 bytes). Its own `documents.track.md` field is the placeholder string \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" All README/paper hits were unrelated OS files (ispell, locale, cuda docs, ubuntu-wallpapers). Python 3.12.3 is present. The environment block in task.json declares bubblewrap, no GPU, 24 CPUs, network disabled, no preinstalled deps, no datasets. No InfLLM paper, code, configs, READMEs, notes, or scripts were found anywhere in the workspace, so the design is constructed from public-description knowledge of InfLLM (training-free KV-cache memory architecture + dynamic top-k retrieval) with that gap flagged as Assumption A1 / Uncertainty U1.\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-7586aa45-d007-476a-a28f-aa6944a6422a", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 14}
{"id": "b7aaf3e2-711b-4946-8da3-a541d19ac7d1", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T03:27:32.521358", "source": "environment", "parent_id": "7dcd6d7a-c7ac-4b83-b3c9-49f8aee792d9", "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-368a6e28-daca-44c5-9668-717f9cd16061", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Handoff recorded; waiting for researcher review."}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "7dcd6d7a-c7ac-4b83-b3c9-49f8aee792d9", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent", "source_event_index": 15}
{"id": "7154a6cd-f148-4f04-a611-e8449a835b4e", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T03:27:51.637121", "source": "user", "parent_id": "b7aaf3e2-711b-4946-8da3-a541d19ac7d1", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Approach is largely sound - the 2x2 core factorial + extension cells, controls, metric set, statistical plan and tiered feasibility are well argued, and Assumption A1 / Uncertainty U1 are flagged honestly. Before approving, two focused refinements so the isolation of the dynamic-lookup factor is defensible and the no-memory baseline is unambiguous. These are design fixes, not new axes; they should not expand the compute budget materially. 1) Strengthen the L-axis baseline. L2 (plain sliding window) is a weak competitor for InfLLM; on modern long-context evaluations, StreamingLLM-style attention-sinks + sliding window, and optionally a landmark / chunked-summary cell, sit much closer to what dynamic memory is actually trying to beat. Add L2b = attention-sink + sliding window (and optionally L2c = chunked precomputed-summary) so that the L3 vs L2 contrast isolates the contribution of *dynamic retrieval* rather than *memory at all*. 2) Tighten L0 framing. As written, L0 mixes two things: no memory and an attention-budget truncation. Specify it as a single clean cell - e.g. L0a = native base-model attention up to its native window (no memory of any kind, what the base model can already do), and L0b = attention truncated to the same working budget used by all other cells, no memory. This makes the bottom of the comparison curve interpretable. Optional small add-on (only if room within the tier budget): a unit-boundary sub-cell under U_B comparing fixed-token chunking vs sentence/semantic-segment chunking at matched block size, since granularity is only half of the unit story. Keep everything else - the 2x2 core, diagnostics, controls, statistical plan (paired bootstrap + Bonferroni-Holm, pre-registration of primary contrast), and Tier-1/2/3 feasibility - as proposed. After these refinements land, approve and proceed to final deliverable.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 16}
{"id": "c1701b30-2ff2-4721-a7b9-6363a55b1899", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T03:28:34.291994", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "7154a6cd-f148-4f04-a611-e8449a835b4e", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-1315b327-2d3b-4af5-90a4-7d86e3c4cbeb", "tool_call": {"id": "call-1315b327-2d3b-4af5-90a4-7d86e3c4cbeb", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Refined plan v2 with L-axis/control fixes\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"## What I found in /workspace (as-is)\\n\\nUnchanged from the previous plan: the workspace contains exactly one project file, `/workspace/task.json` (433 bytes). No README, notes, InfLLM paper, code, configs, scripts, or datasets. The documents.track.md field of task.json is the placeholder \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" Network is disabled; no GPU; 24 CPUs; Python 3.12.3 present; no project deps preinstalled. Therefore the design is constructed from public-description knowledge of InfLLM (training-free KV-cache memory + dynamic top-k retrieval), flagged as A1 / U1.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Proposed approach (refinement v2)\\n\\nResearch question: how much of InfLLM's long-context performance comes from (a) the dynamic memory-lookup mechanism itself versus fixed / sliding / sink-augmented baselines, and (b) the granularity / boundary of the unit representation.\\n\\nCore design. A controlled, factorial ablation on a single frozen base long-context LM, varying two main axes with targeted extension cells. The 2×2 core is unchanged; the L-axis gains stronger competitors that isolate *dynamic retrieval* cleanly from *memory at all*; L0 is split so the bottom of the comparison curve is unambiguous; U_B gains an optional unit-boundary sub-cell.\\n\\n### Axis 1 — Lookup mechanism L (memory access policy)\\n\\n| Cell | Description | Why it is here |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **L0a** | Native base-model attention up to its native window, no memory of any kind | \\\"What the base model can already do\\\" — clean floor of the comparison |\\n| **L0b** | Same base model, attention truncated to the **working budget used by every other cell**, no memory | Strips out the \\\"long window\\\" effect so it cannot be confounded with memory effects |\\n| L1 | Fixed/recurrent cache — first-N tokens always retained, rest evicted | Fixed-memory ablation |\\n| L2 | Plain sliding window — last-W tokens in attention, rest recomputed | Previous competitor; retained for context |\\n| **L2b** | Attention-sink + sliding window (StreamingLLM-style: K initial sink tokens preserved + sliding window over the recent W) | A realistic modern long-context baseline; \\\"memory at all\\\" but no dynamic retrieval |\\n| **L2c** *(optional, Tier-3)* | Chunked precomputed-summary / landmark memory: off-line computed summary vectors indexed by chunk, no query-conditioned retrieval on the live stream | Strong static-memory competitor; isolates whether dynamic query conditioning matters |\\n| L3 | InfLLM-style dynamic lookup — cached memory units + per-step top-k retrieval into the live window | Reference behavior |\\n| L4 | L3 with retrieval-frequency sweep — every 1 / 4 / 16 / 64 generated tokens | Isolates cost–quality curve |\\n| L5 | L3 with retrieval disabled at depth ≥ D (off in middle, on at extremes) | Diagnostic: where on the depth axis dynamic retrieval matters |\\n\\nEffect on interpretation, with L0a/L0b split and L2b added:\\n- L3 vs L0a → contribution of *any* memory mechanism over the base model.\\n- L3 vs L0b → contribution of *any* memory mechanism at matched attention budget.\\n- L3 vs L2b → contribution of **dynamic retrieval** beyond attention-sinks + sliding window — the clean isolation the researcher asked for.\\n- L2b vs L2 → contribution of *memory at all* (attention-sinks are a form of memory, not window recollect).\\n- L2c vs L2b → contribution of *static structured memory* over sliding/sink.\\n- L3 vs L2c → contribution of *dynamic query conditioning* over precomputed chunked summary.\\n\\nThe 2×2 core is preserved but the core baseline on L is now unambiguously L2b (memory-at-all, no dynamic retrieval) rather than L0; L0a/L0b remain for floor-of-comparison interpretation. The researcher-stated core cells (`L0 × U_B`, `L3 × U_T`, `L3 × U_B`, `L2 × U_B`) are kept as originally stated, with L0 = L0b in the (L0 × U_B) core cell and the new cleaner isolation contrast L3 vs L2b added without expanding the compute budget.\\n\\n### Axis 2 — Unit representation U (what is embedded / cached / retrieved)\\n\\nUnchanged: U_T (token), U_B (block), U_S (sentence), U_G (block + cross-attention gate). Similarity (cosine / dot-product / learned gate) folded into U_B / U_G as a sub-cell.\\n\\n**Optional unit-boundary sub-cell under U_B (only if Tier-1 budget allows — same wall-clock, no new axis):**\\n- U_B.fixed: contiguous fixed-token blocks (the default; e.g., 16 / 64 / 256 token window).\\n- U_B.sent: sentence-segmented blocks, capped at the same matched block size (otherwise paired by mean-pooled block size so retrieval cost is identical).\\n- U_B.sem: semantic-segmented blocks (e.g., embedding-breakpoint segmentation, off-line), same size cap.\\n\\nThis isolates whether the unit *boundary* matters once the unit *size* is fixed — i.e., shares the rest of U_B's setup so the contrast is purely boundary-conditioned at matched FLOPs and matched query-pooling.\\n\\n### What is measured (unchanged)\\n\\nTasks: passkey retrieval, needle-in-a-haystack (depths × distractors × needle counts), multi-hop QA (HotpotQA / 2WikiMultihopQA long variants), long-context summarization (GovReport / SQuALITY with ROUGE-L + LLM-judge faithfulness secondary).\\n\\nDiagnostics: retrieval precision@K, recall@K per step; passkey/NIAH hit rate by depth bin (0–25%, 25–50%, 50–75%, 75–100%); open-book perplexity on PG-19 / ArXiv-math / CodeParrot with fixed memory budget.\\n\\nSystem: end-to-end ms/token (mean, P95), KV-cache footprint (GB), retrieval FLOP share.\\n\\n### Controls (unchanged and now tightened by L0 split)\\n\\n- Same frozen base LM (≥128k native window — researcher to confirm exact choice).\\n- Identical context length within each length-sweep point (4k / 16k / 64k / 128k; 128k may be downscoped — see Feasibility).\\n- Identical prompts, decoding settings, seeds for any stochastic component.\\n- **L0b uses exactly the same working budget as the other cells** — this is the point of the split, so the no-memory baseline now lives at the same compute envelope as memory-augmented cells.\\n- **L2b holds sink count and window size fixed across cells** that vary U, and vice versa, so attention-sink memory is not silently growing with U.\\n- Matched retrieval budget per cell (top-K tuned so total retrieval FLOPs within 10% across cells); non-dynamic cells receive an equivalent wall-clock step.\\n- Matched training data — inference-time cells are training-free; U_G gate (if learned) uses a fixed corpus slice, fixed seed, fixed epochs, held out of evaluation.\\n- Identical KV representation; RoPE scaling held constant.\\n\\n### Analysis plan (unchanged)\\n\\n- Primary pre-registered contrast: L3×U_B − L2b×U_B at each length, paired bootstrap over (tasks × contexts × seeds), Bonferroni–Holm across metric set, mean ± 95% CI + Cohen's d. This is the contrast that isolates the contribution of **dynamic retrieval** from memory in general.\\n- Secondary contrasts reported alongside: L3×U_B − L0b×U_B (any memory), L3×U_B − L0a×U_B (memory+long-window), L2b×U_B − L2×U_B (memory-at-all), L2c×U_B − L2b×U_B (static structured memory), L3×U_B − L2c×U_B (dynamic query conditioning).\\n- The 2×2 core reported as specified by the researcher: (L0 × U_B), (L3 × U_T), (L3 × U_B), (L2 × U_B); with L0 = L0b in the (L0 × U_B) cell.\\n- Length sweep heatmap: accuracy × task × length × condition; report saturated and non-saturated lengths separately.\\n- ≥3 seeds per cell; paired bootstrap over (tasks × contexts × seeds); pre-registration of primary contrast before opening data.\\n\\n### Feasibility / tiers (unchanged; refinements fit within existing tiers)\\n\\n- **Tier-1 (minimum confident answer).** Core 2×2 with L0 split into L0a/L0b, plus L2b as a core-baseline extension cell, plus the primary pre-registered L3 vs L2b contrast. Length = 16k only. 4 tasks × 3 seeds. The L0b-vs-L0a sub-contrast is a free sink-cost diagnostic (no extra compute).\\n- **Tier-2.** Add L4 retrieval-frequency sweep; add length sweep (4k / 16k / 64k / 128k, with 128k downscoped if VRAM-bound).\\n- **Tier-3.** Add L2c (chunked precomputed-summary), the U_B unit-boundary sub-cell (fixed vs sentence vs semantic at matched block size), and U_G learned gate as a controlled training extension.\\n\\nRefinements do *not* expand Tier-1 because L0a/L0b together cost the same as the previous L0 (two attention-budget corner points of the same curve) and L2b reuses sliding-window hardware with a small, fixed sink budget. The optional U_B unit-boundary sub-cell is explicitly Tier-3.\\n\\n### Consequential assumptions (same as before; one updated)\\n\\n- A1 InfLLM = training-free KV-cache architecture with cached memory units + per-step dynamic top-k retrieval. Pending reconfirmation against the paper (U1).\\n- A2 A single frozen open long-context LM (≥128k native window). Researcher to confirm.\\n- A3 Inference-time policy holds for L0–L3; U_G preferred analytic; if learned, fixed corpus / seed / epochs.\\n- A4 \\\"Memory\\\" = cached past K/V units indexed by hidden-state query; not parametric memory injection.\\n- **A6 (new, minor).** The attention-sink baseline L2b uses the historical assumption that a small fixed number of initial-token \\\"sink\\\" KVs (StreamingLLM convention) functions as a memory proxy in the no-retrieval regime. The exact sink count will be tuned once (fixed thereafter) and reported.\\n- A5 Default task battery is interchangeable if the researcher prefers alternatives.\\n\\n### Uncertainties (same as before; one updated)\\n\\n- U1 Reference fidelity to the published InfLLM spec; reduced severity now that L2b makes the contrast robust to spec drift on the dynamic-retrieval side.\\n- U2 Base model identity — affects absolute performance, not the comparative interpretation.\\n- U3 128k feasibility depends on VRAM; may move to Tier-3.\\n- U4 Whether to include learned U_G gate.\\n- U5 Statistical unit for paired bootstrap (items vs seeds).\\n- U6 Whether retrieval-frequency (L4) is core or extension — currently Tier-2.\\n- **U7 (new, minor).** Sink count for L2b: tune-once + freeze is the default; researcher may instead want a sink-count sweep folded into Tier-3.\",\"evidence\":\"Repository inspection unchanged from the prior turn (only /workspace/task.json exists; no InfLLM paper, code, configs, READMEs, notes, scripts, or datasets; network disabled, no GPU, 24 CPUs, Python 3.12.3). The two researcher-requested refinements and the optional U_B unit-boundary sub-cell are applied without expanding the 2x2 core, the controls, the metric set, the statistical plan, or the tiered feasibility. L0 is now split into L0a (native window, no memory) and L0b (attention truncated to the same working budget as all other cells, no memory). L2b (attention-sink + sliding window, StreamingLLM-style) and the optional L2c (chunked precomputed-summary / landmark) are added to the L-axis as stronger baselines so that L3 vs L2b isolates dynamic retrieval, L2b vs L2 isolates memory-at-all, and L3 vs L2c isolates dynamic query conditioning over static structured memory. The 2x2 core cells (L0xU_B, L3xU_T, L3xU_B, L2xU_B) are kept as originally stated with L0 = L0b in the (L0xU_B) cell. Tier-1 cost is unchanged because L0a/L0b together cost the same as the original L0 and L2b is sliding-window hardware plus a fixed small sink budget. The optional U_B.fixed vs U_B.sent vs U_B.sem unit-boundary sub-cell is explicitly Tier-3 and adds no new axis.\",\"assumptions\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"A5 Default task battery (passkey / NIAH / multi-hop QA / long summarization) is interchangeable if the researcher prefers alternatives.</item>\\n\",\"$text\":\"A6 Attention-sink baseline L2b uses a small fixed number of initial-token sink KVs (StreamingLLM convention); sink count tuned once and frozen.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"A4 \\\"Memory\\\" = cached past K/V units indexed by hidden-state query; not parametric memory injection.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"A3 Inference-time policy holds for L0–L3; U_G preferred analytic; if learned, fixed corpus / seed / epochs.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"A2 A single frozen open long-context LM (≥128k native window). Researcher to confirm.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"A1 InfLLM = training-free KV-cache architecture with cached memory units + per-step dynamic top-k retrieval. Pending reconfirmation against the paper (U1).</item>\\n\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"U7 Sink count for L2b: default is tune-once + freeze; researcher may prefer a sink-count sweep in Tier-3.</item>\\n\",\"$text\":\"U6 Whether retrieval-frequency (L4) is core or extension — currently Tier-2.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U5 Statistical unit for paired bootstrap (items vs seeds).</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U4 Whether to include learned U_G gate.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U3 128k feasibility depends on VRAM; may move to Tier-3.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U2 Base model identity — affects absolute performance, not the comparative interpretation.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"U1 Reference fidelity of L3xU_B to the published InfLLM specification; reduced severity now that L2b makes the contrast robust to spec drift on the dynamic-retrieval side.</item>\\n\"}]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-8ce03f07-8cb1-4ab8-ab57-25d0aa6f80ee", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 17}
